{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ad97e8e510c5aaca5","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TJBMDLw5BEsiQbYEmiUL5o","description":"Write lz4 streaming diff test","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-FzvpBK\n\nThere are two shared libraries implementing the SAME C API (LZ4 v1.10.0):\n- reference C build: ./cbuild/liblz4.so\n- Rust port under test: ./translation/target/release/liblz4.so\n\nYour job: write ONE new C differential test program at ./tests/diff_stream.c , compile it with\n`gcc -O1 -o tests/diff_stream tests/diff_stream.c -ldl`, run it from the working dir, and report the\nexact failures it finds (do NOT try to fix the Rust code — I will do that; just report precisely).\n\nRequirements for the test program:\n- `dlopen` BOTH .so files with RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL and resolve every function via `dlsym`\n  (never link against lz4 headers; declare function pointer typedefs yourself).\n- For every test, run the SAME sequence of calls against both libraries with identical inputs and\n  compare (a) return values and (b) the produced output bytes, and (c) any in/out parameters.\n- Print a line \"MISMATCH <what> ...\" with enough context (test name, size, mode, block index,\n  return values, first differing byte offset) for each mismatch, and finish with\n  \"checks=<N> fails=<M>\".\n- Use a deterministic xorshift PRNG so both libraries see identical data. Use several data\n  \"modes\": pure random/incompressible, all-identical bytes, short-period repeating, mostly-repeating\n  with random noise, counter bytes (i&0xff), 16-symbol alphabet.\n\nCover these symbols/scenarios thoroughly (this is the LZ4 *block* streaming + dictionary API,\nNOT the LZ4F frame API — ignore all LZ4F_* symbols):\n\nCompression side:\n- LZ4_createStream / LZ4_freeStream / LZ4_initStream / LZ4_resetStream / LZ4_resetStream_fast\n  (check LZ4_initStream returns NULL for NULL buffer, too-small size, misaligned buffer — compare\n   NULL-ness only, not pointer values)\n- LZ4_loadDict, LZ4_loadDictSlow (dict sizes 0,1,3,4,5,64,1000,65535,65536,70000,200000;\n  compare the returned loaded size)\n- LZ4_compress_fast_continue over many successive blocks (contiguous \"prefix\" mode where each\n  block immediately follows the previous in one buffer), with dstCapacity both generous\n  (LZ4_compressBound) and tight (0, 1, small fractions, exact) and accelerations -1,1,2,5,100.\n- Same but \"double buffer\" mode: alternate blocks between two separate buffers.\n- Same but ring-buffer mode: a buffer smaller than 64KB reused circularly.\n- LZ4_loadDict followed by LZ4_compress_fast_continue on a separate (extDict) buffer.\n- LZ4_attach_dictionary: prepare a dict stream with LZ4_loadDict / LZ4_loadDictSlow, attach it to a\n  working stream (freshly reset), then LZ4_compress_fast_continue with block sizes both <= 4KB and\n  > 4KB (both code paths), also attach NULL.\n- LZ4_saveDict (various maxDictSize incl. 0, 4, 1000, 65536, larger than available) — compare\n  return value AND the bytes written into the safe buffer, then continue compressing after it.\n- LZ4_compress_forceExtDict\n- LZ4_compress_fast_extState, LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset (call fastReset repeatedly on the\n  same state so the \"reuse table\" path is exercised), LZ4_compress_destSize_extState with\n  accelerations, LZ4_sizeofState / LZ4_sizeofStreamState / LZ4_resetStreamState / LZ4_create /\n  LZ4_slideInputBuffer (for LZ4_create just check non-NULL and free with LZ4_freeStream;\n  for LZ4_slideInputBuffer compare only whether the returned pointer equals the dictionary pointer\n  you set via LZ4_saveDict, i.e. compare pointer-equality semantics, not raw values)\n- obsolete wrappers: LZ4_compress, LZ4_compress_limitedOutput, LZ4_compress_withState,\n  LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_withState, LZ4_compress_continue, LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_continue\n\nDecompression side (feed it the compressed blocks produced by the C library so both decoders see\nidentical input; also feed deliberately corrupted/truncated blocks to compare error codes):\n- LZ4_createStreamDecode / LZ4_freeStreamDecode / LZ4_setStreamDecode\n- LZ4_decompress_safe_continue across multiple blocks (contiguous, double-buffer, and\n  ring-buffer sized with LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize)\n- LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict, LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict (many targetOutputSize /\n  dstCapacity combinations, including dict adjacent to dst and dict in a separate buffer),\n  LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k, LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict,\n  LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict\n- LZ4_decompress_fast, LZ4_decompress_fast_continue, LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict,\n  LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k  (only with VALID well-formed input, since these are unsafe;\n  use exact original sizes)\n- LZ4_uncompress, LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize\n- LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize over many values incl. negatives and huge, LZ4_versionNumber,\n  LZ4_versionString, LZ4_compressBound over many values incl. negatives and > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE.\n\nIMPORTANT correctness notes for writing the test:\n- LZ4_stream_t is 16416 bytes, LZ4_streamDecode_t is 32 bytes, LZ4_streamHC_t is 262200 bytes.\n  Allocate state buffers with malloc (8-byte aligned) or use the create/free functions.\n- LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE is 0x7E000000.\n- Keep total runtime under ~60 seconds; use buffers up to a few hundred KB, not gigabytes.\n- Do not use any lz4 header file; everything via dlsym.\n- Make sure the program never crashes: guard buffer sizes generously (use LZ4_compressBound from\n  the C lib for compressed buffers, and add slack).\n- If a scenario legitimately produces different results because state is left \"undefined\" after an\n  error (the C docs say a stream is invalid after a failed compression), RESET the stream before\n  reusing it so the comparison stays meaningful.\n\nDeliverables in your final report:\n1. Confirmation that tests/diff_stream.c exists and compiles cleanly (paste the compile command output).\n2. The full stdout of running ./tests/diff_stream (or, if very long, the complete list of distinct\n   MISMATCH lines plus the final checks=/fails= line).\n3. A short list of which scenarios you covered.\nDo not modify anything in c_src/ or translation/.","uuid":"337b5aaa-b1f5-4e79-9d35-534702f691a6","session_id":"2d8fd269-23d7-493b-bff9-939c6c93458e"}
