{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ad97e8e510c5aaca5","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TJBMDLw5BEsiQbYEmiUL5o","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-0pEWtl/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-FzvpBK/2d8fd269-23d7-493b-bff9-939c6c93458e/tasks/ad97e8e510c5aaca5.output","summary":"Compilation is clean and the program runs successfully with `checks=16852 fails=0` in about 0.17 seconds. No mismatches were found between the C reference and the Rust port for any of the scenarios exercised.\n\n## Summary\n\n**File:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-FzvpBK/tests/diff_stream.c` (created, ~1000 lines)\n\n**1. Compile confirmation:**\n```\n$ gcc -O1 -o tests/diff_stream tests/diff_stream.c -ldl\ncompile exit: 0\n```\nNo errors, no warnings.\n\n**2. Full stdout of running `./tests/diff_stream`:**\n```\nchecks=16852 fails=0\n```\nExit code 0. No `MISMATCH` lines were produced — the Rust `liblz4.so` matched the reference C `liblz4.so` bit-for-bit and return-code-for-return-code on every check performed. Runtime ≈0.17s (well under the 60s budget).\n\nOne bug was found and fixed during development of the *test harness itself* (not the libraries under test): a fixed-size stack buffer `unsigned char corrupt[70100]` in the corrupted-input test for `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize` was too small — `LZ4_compressBound(70000)` can be ≈70290 bytes, so the `memcpy` into it caused a stack buffer overflow / segfault. Fixed by allocating the corruption buffer dynamically with `malloc(cmpSize)`. This was purely a test-program defect, unrelated to either library.\n\n**3. Scenarios covered** (all via `dlopen`/`dlsym`, no lz4 headers linked, `LZ4_stream_t`/`LZ4_streamDecode_t` treated as opaque `void*`):\n\nCompression side:\n- `LZ4_createStream`/`freeStream`/`resetStream`/`resetStream_fast`, `LZ4_initStream` NULL/too-small/misaligned edge cases (NULL-ness comparison only)\n- `LZ4_loadDict`/`LZ4_loadDictSlow` across dict sizes {0,1,3,4,5,64,1000,65535,65536,70000,200000}\n- `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`: prefix-mode chains (21 block sizes × 6 data modes × 5 accelerations), tight/generous `dstCapacity` variants, double-buffer mode, ring-buffer mode (<64KB)\n- `LZ4_loadDict` + `compress_fast_continue` on a separate extDict buffer\n- `LZ4_attach_dictionary` (loadDict and loadDictSlow variants, block sizes ≤4KB and >4KB, and NULL attach)\n- `LZ4_saveDict` (sizes 0,4,1000,65536,>available) with byte-content comparison, continued compression afterward, and `LZ4_slideInputBuffer` pointer-equality semantics\n- `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict`\n- `LZ4_compress_fast_extState`, `_fastReset` (repeated reuse), `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState` with accelerations, `LZ4_sizeofState`/`sizeofStreamState`/`resetStreamState`/`LZ4_create`\n- Obsolete wrappers: `LZ4_compress`, `_limitedOutput`, `_withState`, `_limitedOutput_withState`, `_continue`, `_limitedOutput_continue`\n\nDecompression side:\n- `LZ4_createStreamDecode`/`freeStreamDecode`/`setStreamDecode`\n- `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`: contiguous, double-buffer, and ring-buffer (`LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize`-sized) modes, plus corrupted/truncated block error-path comparison with stream recovery via `setStreamDecode(NULL,0)`\n- `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`/`_partial_usingDict` (dict adjacent-to-dst and separate-buffer configurations, multiple targetOutputSize/dstCapacity combos)\n- `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k`, `_forceExtDict`, `_partial_forceExtDict` (empty and real dictionaries)\n- `LZ4_decompress_fast`, `_continue`, `_usingDict`, `_withPrefix64k` (valid well-formed input only)\n- `LZ4_uncompress`, `_unknownOutputSize` (plus a corrupted-input case)\n- `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize`, `LZ4_versionNumber`, `LZ4_versionString`, `LZ4_compressBound` over many values including negatives and values beyond `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (0x7E000000)\n\nData modes used throughout: pure random (incompressible), all-identical bytes, short-period (5-byte) repeating, mostly-repeating-with-noise, counter (`i&0xff`), and 16-symbol alphabet — driven by a deterministic xorshift64 PRNG so both libraries always see identical input bytes.\n\nNo changes were made to `c_src/` or `translation/`; only `tests/diff_stream.c` (and the compiled binary `tests/diff_stream`) were added.","usage":{"total_tokens":146643,"tool_uses":46,"duration_ms":709409},"uuid":"ed3e6794-9f6e-422f-9288-d4fd0f97e150","session_id":"2d8fd269-23d7-493b-bff9-939c6c93458e"}
